local-11: reserve spec-decode blocks per KV cache group for async KV loads (vLLM #59880, in v0.32.0)

With a KV connector loading asynchronously (our CPU tier, local-08), the
scheduler reserves room for the full sequence plus one spec-decode step before
admitting the load. It sized that step with the global block size only, so with
several groups of different block sizes (ours: 20 x 9984 + one 8-token group)
it under-reserved and, under KV pressure, a loaded request could be unable to
start decoding. Now every non-Mamba group is counted with its own block size.
Upstream diff as-is except the last hunk (removal of _spec_decode_step_blocks),
re-anchored for the 0.31 tree. Unit tests (0.31 tests + the PR's): the PR's
multiple-groups and different-block-sizes cases fail before, pass after; the
2 other scheduler failures are pre-existing (PP config validation in the test env).
Drop when the image moves to vLLM >= 0.32.

